<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orissa Tributary States</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Orissa Tributary Mahals</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> Tributary Mahals were the group of small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> in the hills of Orissa, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, that paid tribute to the British after the conquest of 1803. They were supervised by a British superintendent at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a> and from 1933 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-states-agency">Eastern States Agency</a>. In 1948 almost all of them merged into the Indian province of Orissa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orissa-tributary-states.jpg" alt="Orissa Tributary States" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Great Britain India Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orissa_Tributary_States-IGI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
